{
  "id": 20,
  "name": "central_lookahead_return",
  "intent": "Add a mean_remaining-based lookahead that prefers candidates central to the unvisited set early in the tour (weight 0.2 → 0 with progress), anchoring uniform instances near the centroid before return-awareness pulls the closing leg back. Modulate regret by cluster_density so dense regions get a stronger regret signal, and slightly boost nearest_remaining in clusters to preserve clustered performance. Inherits parent's quadratic return ramp and spread-reliability gate. Bounds: rw∈[0.15,0.85], rgw∈[0.009,0.20], lw∈[0,0.2], nw∈[0.05,0.15].",
  "tags": [
    "return_aware",
    "lookahead"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    p = f['progress']\n    s = f['spread']\n    cd = f['cluster_density']\n    rw = 0.15 + 0.4*p + 0.3*p*p\n    rel = s / (0.4 + s + 1e-9)\n    rgw = (0.05 + 0.15*p) * (0.3 + 0.7*rel) * (0.6 + 0.4*cd)\n    lw = 0.2 * (1 - p)\n    nw = 0.05 + 0.1*cd\n    return -f['distance'] + rw*f['return_distance'] + rgw*f['regret'] - lw*f['mean_remaining'] + nw*f['nearest_remaining']",
  "source": "live_llm",
